I changed `GET /invoices/<id>` to return a 404 when the invoice doesn't exist, but I couldn't run it: Flask isn't installed here, so my test request failed on import. There are also no existing tests for this endpoint.

In `src/api/invoices.py`, the handler now returns early when the lookup finds nothing:

```python
invoice = _INVOICES.get(invoice_id)
if invoice is None:
    return problem(404, "Invoice not found", f"No invoice with id {invoice_id!r}")
return jsonify(invoice.__dict__)
```

The 404 uses `problem` from `src/api/errors.py`, which the project uses for all API errors. It sends an `application/problem+json` body with `title` and `detail`. Previously a missing id caused a crash (`None.__dict__`), which showed up as a 500 error.

To check it, install Flask (for example `pip install flask`) and request a missing id with Flask's test client. You should get a 404 with that body.
